<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Futuris half year net profit falls.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Futuris half year net profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>PERTH 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended Dec 31</p>
<p>		  (A$ million unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    22.04 vs  32.50</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		     2.75 vs  2.5</p>
<p>NOTE: Futuris Corp Ltd is a diversified manufacturer and rural services group involved in the manufacture of automotive components, engineering materials and buildings products.  </p>
<p>    Operating profit		  32.51 vs  20.50</p>
<p>    Sales				1,198  vs 194.54</p>
<p>    Other income			29.94 vs  36.05</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			  5.6  vs  10.0</p>
<p>    Abnormal items			nil vs profit 12.00</p>
<p>Dividend is 50 percent franked</p>
<p>Pay date Apr 18</p>
<p>Reg date Apr 4</p>
<p>    Interest			    19.05 vs   4.74</p>
<p>    Depreciation			10.05 vs   6.63</p>
<p>    Shrs (million)		   434.16 vs 297.69</p>
<p>NOTE: Futuris said earnings per share for the previous half year period was adjusted to take into account the one for 10 bonus issue announced with last year's first half profit.</p>
<p>Futuris is in the process of mopping up the outstanding shares in rural services group Elders Australia Ltd after its successful takeover bid.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
